# Internationalization (i18n) Rules

> Rules for implementing multi-language support and localization

## Core Principles

- All user-facing strings must be translatable
- Never hardcode text in components
- Support RTL languages from day 1
- Use standard locale codes (en-US, es-ES, fr-FR, de-DE, ja-JP)

## Technology Stack

- **Next.js**: Use `next-intl` or `react-i18next`
- **React**: React Intl (FormatJS)
- **Translation Management**: Crowdin, Lokalise, or Phrase
- **Date/Time**: `date-fns` with locales or `Intl.DateTimeFormat`
- **Numbers/Currency**: `Intl.NumberFormat`

## File Structure

```
├── messages/
│   ├── en.json      # English (default)
│   ├── es.json      # Spanish
│   ├── fr.json      # French
│   └── de.json      # German
├── i18n/
│   ├── config.ts    # i18n configuration
│   └── utils.ts     # Translation helpers
└── middleware.ts    # Locale detection & routing
```

